{:adr-id "2607158000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-4330 — Building Completion and Finishing Operations-Coordination Actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :context
 "ISIC 4330 (Building completion and finishing -- plastering, painting,
  glazing, floor/wall tiling, finish carpentry) had a :spec-only placeholder
  pointing at a never-created gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-F4330 repo (gh api 404
  confirmed at both the stale placeholder and the real cloud-itonami org
  before any work began). Lower physical-risk trade domain than the
  demolition/road-rail siblings it mirrors structurally -- no heavy
  equipment near public traffic, no structural-collapse risk from the
  actor's own coordinated work; relevant hazards are scaffold/fall risk and
  pre-existing materials hazards (lead paint, asbestos) disturbed by
  renovation."
 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4330 mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-4311
  (Demolition) module-for-module: Finishing Advisor ⊣ Finishing Governor +
  audit ledger. Eight HARD gates: unknown op, effect-not-propose, forbidden
  action class (trade-equipment-control/direct-actuation/structural-
  completion-sign-off), site-not-verified, legal-basis-missing, hazmat-
  survey-incomplete, fall-protection-noncompliant, unresolved-safety-
  concern. MemStore/DatomicStore backends, fully portable .cljc with NO JVM
  interop anywhere in src/ (finishing.notify uses a caller-injected
  function transport seam instead of embedding java.net.http, unlike
  earlier sibling actors). Deliberate difference from 4311/4210:
  :schedule-finishing-operation is NOT a permanent high-stakes member --
  MAY auto-commit at phase 3 when clean+confident, reflecting trade-
  finishing's materially lower risk profile than demolition/heavy-civil
  earthwork scheduling. Per-jurisdiction (JPN/USA/DEU) pre-work hazmat-
  survey + fall-protection legal-basis catalog, every citation
  independently verified via WebFetch/WebSearch against its official
  source (osha.gov, ecfr.gov, laws.e-gov.go.jp, eur-lex.europa.eu,
  baua.de) before being written."
 :consequences
 ["Certified building-finishing operators fork and deploy independently with auditable coordination records; trade-equipment control and structural-completion sign-off remain permanent, un-overridable HARD blocks"
  "First coordination-only actor in this fleet whose own schedule op is deliberately lower-stakes than its structural siblings' -- template for future trade-craft (vs heavy-civil) construction verticals to differentiate risk tiers honestly"
